Key takeaways for a cybersecurity student
VSS = Point-in-time snapshots of a Windows volume.
It allows backups of files that are currently in use.
It relies on three components: Requester → Writer → Provider.
It uses Copy-on-Write, making snapshots space-efficient.
It underpins System Restore, Previous Versions, and many backup solutions.
Forensics teams use VSS to recover deleted or older versions of files.
Ransomware frequently deletes VSS snapshots to prevent recovery.
Penetration testers and attackers may use VSS to obtain consistent copies of locked system files such as NTDS.dit and registry hives.
